# Import and source-extraction audit

Date: 2026-08-29
Scope: `AutomaticCompiledNativeSource`, `AutomaticCompiledNativeFrameworkLoader`, Tailwind/Bootstrap/plain CSS loading, and the browser measurement hand-off.

## Findings before remediation

### P1 — nested ZIP stylesheet references were dropped

Reproduction: ZIP entry `pages/index.html` referenced `../css/site.css`. The source workspace contained the stylesheet. `SourcePackage::filePath()` resolved every path from the workspace root and rejected `..`, so the loader returned `stylesheet-not-found`, omitted the CSS, and measurement saw the section without its real Grid/layout rules.

Observed output:

```json
{"entry":"pages/index.html","diagnostics":[{"code":"stylesheet-not-found","href":"../css/site.css"}],"cssHasGrid":false}
```

Impact: nested ZIP pages were not measured in their actual CSS universe.

### P1 — external stylesheet could be mistaken for a local file

Reproduction: an external `https://cdn.example.com/style.css` link was processed through `filePath()` before external URL classification. With a local `style.css` in the ZIP, the external stylesheet was silently inlined and removed from the HTML; `externalStylesheets` became empty.

Impact: the CSS universe could be incorrect and external provenance was lost.

### P2 — plain `.grid` class was a Tailwind false positive

Reproduction: a plain stylesheet defined `.grid { display: grid; ... }`. Auto detection saw the generic `grid` token and selected `tailwind_static` even though the page had no Tailwind marker.

Impact: a Tailwind reset/base bundle could be injected into ordinary CSS pages and alter measured typography/box-model behavior.

## Passing controls observed during the audit

- Inline CSS, Tailwind static utility compilation, Tailwind arbitrary values, Bootstrap CSS package loading, script/handler/javascript-URL removal, ZIP traversal rejection, and critical stylesheet fail-closed behavior had passing focused coverage.
- Browser measurement uses JavaScript disabled and captures computed styles plus rectangles at desktop/tablet/mobile.

## Remediation gate

The three findings above must be fixed with regression tests before the Canvas workflow tasks are considered valid. Existing v2.4/v2.3 engine files remain out of scope.
